cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite it using the metadata below (the Zenodo DOI identifies the exact version)."
type: software
title: "CRA-SME Toolkit: a risk-driven, evidence-based research toolkit for EU Cyber Resilience Act implementation in SMEs"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Torstensson
    given-names: Olga
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/cra-sme-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Research toolkit for implementing and evaluating the EU Cyber Resilience Act
  (Regulation (EU) 2024/2847) in small and medium-sized enterprises. It contains
  a 46-obligation CRA requirements catalogue, a risk and evidence workbook, a
  tested Python core (ordinal and Monte Carlo risk models, inter-rater
  agreement statistics, SBOM and scanner accuracy metrics, Article 14 reporting
  clocks, a traceability schema with a score-independent release gate, and an
  evidence provenance manifest), a SHA-pinned CI evidence workflow, protocols
  for eight experiments (E1-E8), executed Jupyter notebooks, and an SBOM
  generator pilot benchmark. Research instruments only: not legal advice and
  not a conformity assessment.
keywords:
  - Cyber Resilience Act
  - Regulation (EU) 2024/2847
  - SME
  - SBOM
  - compliance as code
  - cybersecurity risk assessment
  - evidence traceability
  - vulnerability disclosure
  - design science research
